ok I am not saying you didn't make that better, but that didn't change those glyphs back. I am also using konsole terminal, if that makes any difference. I also noticed that theres some sets or individual glyphs that are rendered as a colorful emoji version, which i hate. for example the zodiac signs.

Claude:
Both of those problems are the same underlying issue, just two flavors of it:

Noto Color Emoji is winning when it shouldn't — it's grabbing zodiac signs, rendering them as colorful cartoon 
emoji instead of the clean text/symbol glyphs
Something other than Noto Color Emoji is winning when it should — the moon phases are still getting stolen by
 whatever wrong font had planes and computers in it
Konsole specifically is the key detail. Konsole uses Qt's font stack directly and is notoriously stubborn about
 emoji/symbol resolution. It often ignores fontconfig aliases and only respects explicit per-application rules or 
 its own profile font settings.

Before we go further, I need to know what's actually installed and what fontconfig is currently doing on your 
system so we can diagnose precisely rather than guess. Can you run these and paste the output? 


# What fonts do you have installed that touch symbol/emoji ranges?
fc-list | grep -iE "emoji|symbol|noto|deja|unifont|symbola|quivira|free" | sort

# What actually wins for the moon phase U+1F311?
fc-match --sort :charset=0x1F311 | head -10

# What wins for a zodiac sign e.g. Aries U+2648?
fc-match --sort :charset=0x2648 | head -10

# What does your current fontconfig mess look like?
cat ~/.config/fontconfig/fonts.conf 2>/dev/null || echo "no user config"
ls /etc/fonts/conf.d/




